t03.modifications=[{element:'PPAP Due Date / SubmissionDate (928f4637-0e14-46dc-89bc-90cb6e3fadd2; APQP & PPAP Manager package /GraphData/Items/249)',change:'The package defaults to Task.Workflow.DueDate. Keep its required Date type and timezone setting. For target records remove that unconditional default: require the SIA PPAP Engineer to supply the date at Draft creation, or let the authorized APQP launch copy a valid linked Task due date once. Historical records retain the original branch.'},{element:'PPAP DisplayField (998bd167-41b8-46bf-bc08-b1baa5ec3a50; /GraphData/Items/579)',change:'The package uses CONCATENATE("PPAP ",Product," - ",Product.Name) and exports no maximum. For target records set maximum 512 characters and a continuing display calculation from inherited RecordNo, Drawing Number and Drawing Revision Code in that order, separated by " / "; omit empty context components and never silently truncate identity. Keep the historical Product-based branch; supported executable syntax is a supplied input.'}];
t03.steps=['Arrange the internal Draft controls around Manufacturing Facility, Drawing Revision/Engineering Release, Type, selected Parts, Shipping Depots, Template and responsibility. Label the existing Project Owner control SIA PPAP Engineer in the target view; it remains the same existing field and always represents an internal user.','Limit selected parts to the authoritative drawing/revision and release. Require Source Release Part.Part to equal the selected Part, its release to equal PPAP.Engineering Release and that release Drawing Revision to equal the PPAP Drawing Revision. Copy Part Number, Part Description and all three criticality values; never provide PPAP criticality overrides.','Keep manufacturing facility, drawing/revision, selected parts and authoritative flags read only after issue. Keep a depot separate from approved manufacturing scope; adding contextual depot routing does not grant facility access.','Show both mass controls to authorized supplier users while PPAP is In Progress. Require each actual mass >0 and metal mass >=0 and <= actual mass before final submission, with kilograms displayed; NULL is unknown, metal 0 means confirmed no metal. Hide internal management content. Finalization owns the final server-side completeness check.'];
t03.accept=['A selected source part from another part, release or drawing revision is rejected instead of supplying its flags to the PPAP.','A target Draft can use a supplied overall date with no Task link; its label no longer depends on singular Product.','Actual mass 1.2 and metal mass 0 are valid; metal 1.3 against actual 1.2 is rejected; missing mass is not converted to zero.'];

