t31.steps=['Configure each proposed target branch by resolving the exact PPAP record and reading Target Configuration?, using the supplied native method; base handlers cannot simply assume a descendant field is accessible. Put the branch check before each named legacy write. Keep the default/historical marker FALSE.','Use the target marker as the condition that bypasses legacy generation. The Create Target PPAP Draft assignment alone owns writing the marker before creation/default processing and selecting the new workflow; do not add another initializer or call that creation operation again from the old handler.','Do not assign changes to legacy listeners already excluded by these early checks unless an actual remaining invocation path is supplied. Keep Copy Values on Create and Create PPAP unchanged: its package operation only fills DefId and does not establish a usable PPAP creation process.'];
t31.accept=['A marked target Draft does not generate old project checklist/tasks or alter legacy phase helpers.','An unmarked historical/APQP record continues through the original handlers; the inherited task/phase definitions are not rebuilt.'];

const t32=task(32,'Restrict PPAP records, decisions and files','Record and file permissions','Give each user only the PPAP information and actions allowed by entity, classification and stage.','Enable governed PPAP audit/security and configure new record/field/attachment rules across supplier/internal work, history and closure. Apply controlled visibility-only handover and direct-access enforcement without duplicating shared SRM or platform permissions.','A target PPAP permission set with protected files/history and controlled visibility handover.',[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,11,12,17,24,25,29],[['IN-05','Supply approved operational groups/roles and current-member rules; client administrators maintain those records/memberships.'],['IN-06','Supply exact visibility values, native record/file/action/export methods, external actor connection and authorized handover principals.'],['IN-13','Supply native file protection that prevents replacement/deletion of frozen evidence and posted attachments.']],{blockedStatus:'Waiting: actual record/file/classification rules require supplied native enforcement methods and approved principals. Earlier tasks provide the full linked record/field graph.'});
t32.modifications=[{element:'PPAP / APQP_PPAPAbstractObject (a99ca3b8-48ed-43eb-9696-a1dd26122c39; /GraphData/Items/45)',change:'The package declares IsAuditEnabled=FALSE and IsSecurityEnabled=FALSE, while inherited effective grants remain unverified. Enable governed audit/security for the retained PPAP using the supplied target/historical access connection. Do not infer safe file access from read-only view markup or rebuild inherited Project Framework security.'}];
t32.steps=['Configure target access as the intersection of authenticated account, application/object/record rights, exact supplier-entity scope, visibility classification, central supplier capability and current stage/action. Assignment and notification recipients alone confer no rights. Keep all Draft content/files unavailable to supplier users.','For authorized supplier coordinator members after Issue, permit supplier-visible scope/status, Confirm Scope, assigned SUPPLIER work/answers/files and part masses while In Progress, plus permitted external discussion. Deny internal elements/comments/management exchanges and prior rejected internal evidence. Other supplier viewers need their separate actual grants and gain no approval rights.','For the responsible internal SIA PPAP Engineer, permit scoped Draft setup/Issue, internal work, element review/self-review, accepted results, permitted reassignment/dates and reasoned cancellation. For eligible management approvers permit only their explicit Management Review decisions; administrator membership does not imply management-pool membership. Inspectors/team owners can complete their work but cannot approve merely through ownership.','For every new operational record and attachment, follow its owning PPAP/element/thread context through declared links. Reused From is internal lineage navigation only and cannot open source-record access. Preserve original submitted/approved/rejected files and posted attachments; deny direct API/import/URL/export/search edits and cross-supplier/classification downloads.','After Issue deny scope, revision, part, classification and requirement-set changes for all roles, including administrators. After approval/cancellation deny business-content edits, deletion, reopen/withdrawal and all discussion posting. Approved evidence remains protected while open correction creates fresh working content; no automatic retention deletion is configured.','Configure the authorized visibility-handover action to change only the shared Visibility Classification on applicable PPAPs and governed descendants, under supplied management authority and native safe-update rules. Audit old/new classification and actor/time; do not change criticality, workflow stage, owner, dates, approved bytes or scope. Allow this security-only change on closed records without allowing ordinary closed-content edits.','Apply the same record/field/file rules to forms, direct URLs, APIs/imports, search, exports and related-record navigation. Use native workflow/audit/notification/execution facilities as provided; add no custom audit/status/processing-permission setup.'];
